  "title": "Three ports are free; junctions cost a factor two",
  "subject": "Where counting on hypergraphs with Pfaffian incidence graphs leaves polynomial time",
  "conclusion": "For 3-regular 3-uniform hypergraphs with Pfaffian incidence graphs, any signs and any weight per monochromatic edge, three-edge tight cuts cost nothing and each 4-sum junction violating the matchgate identity costs at most a factor two at its piece. For 2-colourings only junctions at or above squares with three twisted branches violate it, so counting takes time poly(n) 2^b, between the polynomial unbranched case and the #P-hard branched one.",
